{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile achieves the best performance (0.653 acc, 0.628 F1), while image-only models are extremely weak (0.208–0.227 acc) regardless of encoder. The critical unresolved question is whether adding the image modality via fusion can improve upon the strong RNA-only baseline, or whether the weak image signal is simply noise that will degrade performance. This experiment tests multimodal fusion (weighted) with the proven best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and resnet50. Weighted fusion is the most informative choice here because it can downweight the weak image channel, making it the fairest test of whether image carries any complementary signal. If config_031 fails to exceed 0.653, it provides strong evidence that the image modality is uninformative for this task and the search should focus on RNA-only refinements; if it does exceed it, it justifies further multimodal exploration. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the central design question (is multimodality worth pursuing?) before committing budget to the many remaining multimodal variants."
}

